#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:5
msgid "Stats Collection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:7
msgid ""
"Scrapy provides a convenient facility for collecting stats in the form of "
"key/values, where values are often counters. The facility is called the "
"Stats Collector, and can be accessed through the :attr:`~scrapy.crawler."
"Crawler.stats` attribute of the :ref:`topics-api-crawler`, as illustrated by "
"the examples in the :ref:`topics-stats-usecases` section below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:13
msgid ""
"The Stats Collector API is always available, so you can always use it (to "
"increment or set new stat keys), regardless of whether the stats collection "
"is enabled or not. If it's disabled, the API will still work but it won't "
"collect anything. This is aimed at simplifying the stats collector usage: "
"you should spend no more than one line of code for collecting stats in your "
"spider, Scrapy extension, or whatever code you're using the Stats Collector "
"from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:21
msgid ""
"Another feature of the Stats Collector is that it's very efficient (when "
"enabled) and extremely efficient (almost unnoticeable) when disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:24
msgid "See :ref:`topics-stats-reference` below for the stats that Scrapy sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:29
msgid "Common Stats Collector uses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:31
msgid ""
"Access the stats collector through the :attr:`~scrapy.crawler.Crawler.stats` "
"attribute. Here is an example of an extension that access stats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:34
msgid ""
"class ExtensionThatAccessStats:\n"
"    def __init__(self, stats):\n"
"        self.stats = stats\n"
"\n"
"    @classmethod\n"
"    def from_crawler(cls, crawler):\n"
"        return cls(crawler.stats)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:46
msgid "Set stat value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:48
msgid "stats.set_value(\"hostname\", socket.gethostname())"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:52
msgid "Increment stat value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:54
msgid "stats.inc_value(\"custom_count\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:58
msgid "Set stat value only if greater than previous:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:60
msgid "stats.max_value(\"max_items_scraped\", value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:64
msgid "Set stat value only if lower than previous:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:66
msgid "stats.min_value(\"min_free_memory_percent\", value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:70
msgid "Get stat value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:72
msgid ""
">>> stats.get_value(\"custom_count\")\n"
"1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:77
msgid "Get all stats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:79
msgid ""
">>> stats.get_stats()\n"
"{'custom_count': 1, 'start_time': datetime.datetime(2009, 7, 14, 21, 47, 28, "
"977139)}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:87
msgid "Available Stats Collectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/stats.rst:91
msgid ""
"Besides the basic :class:`StatsCollector` there are other Stats Collectors "
"available in Scrapy which extend the basic Stats Collector. You can select "
"which Stats Collector to use through the :setting:`STATS_CLASS` setting. The "
"default Stats Collector used is the :class:`MemoryStatsCollector`."
msgstr ""

